# rule.always.converge-with-reviewers.via-a-taken-per-point

for EVERY `.given.by_peer` point author the paired `.taken.by_self` before you re-arrive. every round.

- `[REPAIR]` ("i fixed it"): quote the **current** file
- `[REFUTE]` ("it does not hold"): cited evidence (out of scope, false positive, deliberate tradeoff)

then per point: `rhx route.stone.set --stone <stone> --as absorbed --that <slug>`, and only then re-arrive.

a blocker that returns after your fix is a driver error: check whether you ever told the reviewer.

on an APPROVED lane, `--as absorbed` with no `.taken` warns and does not refuse. only a `.taken` discharges a point.

blocker: an open point with no `.taken` · a `[REPAIR]` with no current-file quote · a `[REFUTE]` with no evidence · a malfunction graded for a re-raise you never answered · a re-arrival with an open approved-lane point and no `.taken`.
twin: `rule.forbid.unanswered-exits-from-a-blocker`.
